.0,"min_p":0.02,"repeat_penalty":1.02,"temperature":0.9,"top_p":0.97,"xtc_probability":0.1},"seed":1312037,"source_ids":["apprenticeship.wharton.age-of-innocence.c001.s022","apprenticeship.wharton.age-of-innocence.c001.s010","apprenticeship.forster.room-with-a-view.c003.s001"],"span":{"call_id":"runway.parallel-book-continuity.fulcrum-s01.1312037","raw_char_end":929,"raw_char_start":0,"raw_hash":"a508f262d3c11acb31ce9560c97578eb24bdf52bb00851eff87bf5b887657721","raw_path":"03_scene_lab/runs/prompt-autoresearch-v42-s01-concrete-openings/runways/raw/runway.parallel-book-continuity.fulcrum-s01.1312037.txt","role":"opening-runway","span_id":"runway.parallel-book-continuity.fulcrum-s01.1312037","text_hash":"dc19d7e86426f2d58b1a210e272b198d8c2013f1b3c619108792431a25104168"},"status":"completed","text":"Mara entered the rideshare after waiting outside her apartment building\nfor twenty-four minutes, ten of them in a rain so brief and sudden she\nhad no time to put up her umbrella. The car felt hot and stuffy, as it\nmight when parked for a long time with the windows up. Mara opened both\nthe doors, and the smell of the previous passenger, faint and vaguely\nfamiliar, leaked into the cool night air. The car didn't feel\nespecially clean; Mara didn't mind.\n\nAs the car pulled away from the curb, the driver asked, \"How long you\nbeen at Fulcrum?\" His name was George. Mara told him she had just\narrived.\n\nHe laughed. \"Just arrived? I bet you have been at least eight or ten\nyears. And you are about twenty-three.\" Mara could see that George took\npleasure in these kinds of statements, which he apparently made often,\neven though they were seldom correct, even approximately.\n\n\"You're not quite right,\" said Mara. \"I've just arrived.\"","text_hash":"dc19d7e86426f2d58b1a210e272b198d8c2013f1b3c619108792431a25104168","timings":{"cache_n":4360,"predicted_ms":69317.983,"predicted_n":260,"predicted_per_second":3.7508304302506903,"predicted_per_token_ms":266.6076269230769,"pr